00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:07.829 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  i've worked 40 years in the council  secretariat and this will be the sixth  job that i have in the organization  and before that i was a swedish diplomat  for a few years and i studied law in  sweden  after my  studies  this job is about  the organization of all the official  meetings and events in the council  buildings so  the protocol and meetings directorate  coordinates these activities we're big  directors 200 people with a big budget  and we cooperate with all the services  in the gse on a daily basis so it's very  sociable and very dynamic  there isn't really a typical day in this  job  except that when in brussels i do have  many meetings  but it's with very different  interlocutors  it can be discovery day when welcoming  newcomers to the directorate but it can  also be with  belgian authorities to prepare big  events in brussels it can be on a  mission  abroad preparing  a visit of the president of the european  council  or being on the mission with him so  usually i know roughly what i'm going to  do when i arrive at work but sometimes  it doesn't turn out that way at all  and my previous posts have prepared me  for this job i think uh as a swedish  diplomat i participated in uh  sweden's first presidency of the council  so i have that perspective  i had several jobs as an aed in  different parts of the house  and my first management job was in the  swedish language unit  and there i learned really many things  but in particular the crucial importance  of the language issue in the council be  it in writing like for the translators  or orally as we need interpreters for  many of our meetings  and of course as head of the protocol  unit for the past three years i've also  learned a lot about the activities of  org ii and how we work with others so i  benefit from that now  and sometimes there are unexpected  things in the job  such as when  i accompanied the president tusk on a  visit to the border between tajikistan  and afghanistan he was going  the authorities were bringing him there  to  to look at the the work that they're  doing and he was also going to be  offered a lunch  fortunately i was not wearing heels flat  shoes but they were still just work in  ballerinas and you had to climb down in  uh like a gravel slope that was very  steep and it's also very high so it was  not so easy to breathe uh  but i managed that but the shoes were  completely ruined of course  so in org two  we coordinate the meetings that  should provide a good setting for  negotiations and also a good image of  the political stakeholders involved but  there's an enormous amount of  behind the scenes work involved so  the 200 staff in orbit are very busy  making sure that everything runs  smoothly  once the  the guests are here  but  i could talk a long time about all the  small steps that need to be taken by  many many people not just in org two but  also in other gse services  to make all this look perfect when it  takes place  this job is sometimes quite intense so i  do need to recharge at the end of the  day  and here i very often exercise and i  also enjoy cooking for my family this is  a kind of mental rest for me and  recently i went to a classical concert  again  for the first time in two years because  of kovid and this is something i need to  do more of too  [Music]  you

